                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e45ed846-e40f-3c27-8f06-952758a77b60",
                        "entry_id": "d7ec6d6f-b48b-3f40-8adc-5773295008fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To enrol (jurors), e.g. from a jury pool; to register (the names of jurors) on a \\\"panel\\\" or official list."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "faa4e503-2c34-45fc-bb23-c8afa81e9dc1",
                                "sense_id": "e45ed846-e40f-3c27-8f06-952758a77b60",
                                "text": "To 'cide this title is impannelled / A quest of thoughts, all tenants to the heart; / And by their verdict is determined / The clear eye's moiety, and the dear heart's part"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d5c28eb-34b4-4a3c-a9af-d650e5bc5b60",
                                "sense_id": "e45ed846-e40f-3c27-8f06-952758a77b60",
                                "text": "Therefore a Jurie was impaneld streight / T'enquire of them, whether by force, or sleight, / Or their owne guilt, they were away conveyd?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "703b9418-1508-432d-b8da-81e0ac1329b2",
                                "sense_id": "e45ed846-e40f-3c27-8f06-952758a77b60",
                                "text": "We are often driven to empanell and select a jury of twelve men out of a whole countrie to determine of an acre of land[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58ae540a-7014-4ec7-a2c3-7526b9460b71",
                                "sense_id": "e45ed846-e40f-3c27-8f06-952758a77b60",
                                "text": "...placed him under the decent and disagreeable necessity of returning at once, before a bet was decided, whether his own cook, or that of Lord Montagle's, would prepare a single dish to the greatest perfection. The jury of taste had been impanelled, and here was he summoned away ten minutes before the dishes came up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ad0e04d-0b5b-4323-b2eb-8693cdede516",
                                "sense_id": "e45ed846-e40f-3c27-8f06-952758a77b60",
                                "text": "In the courtroom itself they were empaneling a jury."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
